# Proposed by the swarm's review (2026-10-14); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: a laptop user is zoomed in on Safari when they plug in a monitor to the
# right. Notes, docked and parked past the right edge, must not show up on it. The Calculator floats: no view
# takes it away and no monitor moves it.
# Reference: T44 T52 T61.
# The three tiling switches of the guide's section 2 are off: with macOS's own tiling on, the left, right and top edges of the screen are macOS's (Q23).
mac-tiling off
open Safari
open Notes
open Calculator 300x400
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
zoom 101
expect hidden 102
expect still 103
expect visible 103
expect at 103 300 200 300x400
displays 2
expect hidden 102
expect still 103
expect visible 103
expect at 103 300 200 300x400
expect fills 101
back
expect visible 102
expect still 103
expect visible 103
expect at 103 300 200 300x400
# Notes moves to the monitor, which is then unplugged and plugged back in.
drag 102 1445 500 cmd
expect docked 102
displays 1
expect floating 102
expect visible 102
displays 2
expect docked 102
expect visible 102
# Only floating windows that make way leave with the Desktop. Out of view, the Calculator must not show up on the monitor either.
displays 1
cursor 400 400
set floatingWindowsMakeWay true
zoom 101
expect hidden 103
displays 2
expect hidden 103
expect fills 101
back
expect visible 103
